                        "entry_id": "78d7c071-d723-31b8-9740-4a92dbe9a68f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A former Turkish unit of weight equal to 100 dirhems (variously 0.15–0.35 kg)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e028dc68-50a2-416a-8b01-730b0bc45681",
                                "sense_id": "e2f11883-73cf-3266-ac91-d3f5120c4c69",
                                "text": "At Constantinople, the cantaro, or quintal, contains 44 okes, or 100 rottoli; and the cantaro weighs about 123¾ lbs. avoirdupois, the oke 2lbs. 13 oz., and the rottolo 19⁴⁄₅ oz., and the chequee 11¼ oz. avoirdupois."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b1031008-b582-49bf-8f15-ac5a618d2fba",
                                "sense_id": "e2f11883-73cf-3266-ac91-d3f5120c4c69",
                                "text": "Dram (49·5 grains), 100=chequi, 4=oka (2·8286 ℔); dram (49·5 grains), 180=rotl, 100=kintal or kantar (127·29 ℔)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "744b30a1-608d-4504-8598-9beb4379d304",
                                "sense_id": "e2f11883-73cf-3266-ac91-d3f5120c4c69",
                                "text": "6107. Turkish Weights. The Turkish Chequi is 11⅓ ounces avoirdupois... 1 Chequi = 100 Drachmas."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
